    "description": "Objective: support the CMS→Salesforce inbound integration for Deal Rep Assignments, per the 2026-07-28 decision (CMS owns rep-assignment execution; SF is system of record for assignment history and performance tracking).\n\nScope (SF side):\n\n* Field contract: CMS upserts Deal_Rep_Assignment\\__c on DRA_Temp_Ext_Id_\\_c (external ID) with Deal External ID, Rep External ID, Assignment Status, Effective From/To, Link Slug, Assignment_Source = API\n\n* Effective_From__c immutable on update (CMS must not overwrite on status change)\n\n* Status-transition payload handling (Active → Ended etc.); DRA History continues via existing after-save flow\n\n* Error semantics: reject vs Review Required — align with contract in requirements doc (BUILD-67)\n\n* Integration user permissions for DRA object (verify WT_DealRepAssignment_Edit on integration user)\n\nBLOCKED BY: Wagertech (Joyce) building the CMS-side caller once the requirements doc (BUILD-67, due 7/31) is delivered.\n\nNOTE: the original SF→CMS outbound (deal publish) direction was split to BUILD-66. Fallback if this misses go-live: SF Manage Assignment flow (BUILD-45, optional).\n\nHistory: originally scoped as one-way SF→CMS push; direction reversed at the 2026-07-28 weekly sync. Part of Epic — CMS ↔ SF Integration.",
